# Supabase is entirely optional. IndexedDB (in the browser) is the primary
# datastore and the app works fully offline without any of these set.
#
# Configuring Supabase enables:
#  - Cross-device player identity matching (same IP, different browser)
#  - Cloud backup of finalized daily betting records
#  - Accounts / subscriptions / admin dashboard (see below)
#
# See README.md "Supabase (optional)" for the SQL to create these tables.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Accounts / subscriptions / admin dashboard (optional) -----------------
# All three below are SERVER-ONLY secrets — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_,
# never expose to the browser bundle.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: from Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API
# > service_role key. Used exclusively by src/app/api/admin/* route handlers
# to make privileged writes (another user's subscription tier, app_settings)
# after independently verifying the caller's session role is 'admin'. Never
# reaches the client.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ADMIN_EMAILS: comma-separated allowlist. On signup, if the account's email
# is in this list, its profile row is created with role='admin' — this is
# how you bootstrap the first admin account without hand-editing the
# database. Safe to leave unset until you're ready to grant admin access.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# Note: guest-mode on/off, the active metering mode (coin vs time), and all
# tier/guest limit numbers live in the `app_settings` table (defaults are
# set by supabase/schema.sql's insert), editable from /admin — not env vars.
# Accounts/subscriptions are entirely unavailable until the two Supabase
# vars above are set, same as every other Supabase-gated feature here.
